#[doc("""
What a run says when it did not get through what it planned.

A pool that runs out of kalku ends the run, and the wekufe it had not cast
are not measured. The ones it did cast were, and they are reported — but a
report of them alone carries a score and a clean exit, so a CI job or an
agent reads a finished run. Saying where it stopped, and why, in the
report and in the exit code, is the only honest answer. An interrupt is
the same answer: the wekufe it kept from being cast were not measured.
""")]

#[doc("""
What ended a casting early, if anything: what the pool said, or else the
interrupt that cancelled it.
""")]
pub fn what_ended(failure: Option[String], cancelled: Bool) : Option[String] =
  failure |> or_else(() => if cancelled { Some("it was interrupted") } else { None })

#[doc("""
Why a run is not a measurement, when it stopped before casting everything:
how far it got and what the pool said. `None` when it got through its plan,
whatever the pool said on the way out, since nothing was left unmeasured.
""")]
pub fn stopped_short(failure: Option[String], cast: Int, planned: Int) : Option[String] =
  failure
    |> and_then(
      why => if cast < planned {
        Some("the run stopped after #{cast} of #{planned} wekufe: #{why}")
      } else {
        None
      }
    )
